Mods and assets
---------------

Everything under mods/ is excluded from the tooling licence, including mod
definitions, scripts, artwork, audio, maps, screenshots and documentation.
Each mod remains governed by the licence declared in its mod.json and its
accompanying licence and attribution notices. Its creators and other
respective rights holders retain ownership. Inclusion in this repository,
a generated index or a release package does not transfer ownership or
relicense any mod or asset.

Submission permissions are described in CONTRIBUTING.md. They give the
registry specific operational permissions without replacing a mod's public
licence or granting the public additional reuse rights.

Earlier releases
----------------

The tooling licence change takes effect with the commit introducing this
notice. It does not revoke permissions already granted for material
previously released under MIT or another licence. The previous MIT licence
and copyright notice are retained in LICENSES/MIT-legacy.txt for that
material; they do not offer MIT as an alternative for new material released
only under PolyForm Strict. Existing mod licences remain unchanged.

Nothing here limits rights granted by applicable law or GitHub's terms for
viewing and forking a public repository on GitHub.
